Interview Questions
Q1. Why Controller?

Handles incoming HTTP requests and delegates business logic to the Service layer.

Q2. Why should Controller not contain business logic?

To maintain Separation of Concerns. Business logic belongs in the Service layer.

Q3. Why @RestController instead of @Controller?

@Controller

Returns a View (JSP, Thymeleaf).

@RestController

Returns JSON/XML directly.
Used for REST APIs.
Q4. Why @RequestMapping?

Defines the base URL for all APIs in the controller.

Q5. Difference between @RequestMapping and @GetMapping?
@RequestMapping → Generic mapping (can specify any HTTP method).
@GetMapping → Specifically maps HTTP GET requests.
