-------------------------------------Response Entity----------------------------------------------
ResponseEntity
Purpose

ResponseEntity gives complete control over the HTTP response.

It lets us return:

Response Body
HTTP Status Code
Headers
Why not return an object directly?
public User createUser(...)

Spring automatically returns:

200 OK

You cannot easily customize the status code.

With ResponseEntity
public ResponseEntity<User> createUser(...)

Now you can return any status code.

Common Examples
GET
return ResponseEntity.ok(user);

Status

200 OK
POST
return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(user);

Status

201 CREATED
DELETE
return ResponseEntity.noContent().build();

Status

204 NO CONTENT
NOT FOUND
return ResponseEntity.notFound().build();

Status

404 NOT FOUND
Flow
Controller
      ↓
ResponseEntity
      ↓
HTTP Status + Body + Headers
      ↓
Client
Interview Questions
Q1. What is ResponseEntity?

ResponseEntity is a wrapper around the HTTP response that allows us to customize the response body, status code, and headers.

Q2. Why use ResponseEntity?

It allows us to return appropriate HTTP status codes like 201 Created, 404 Not Found, and 204 No Content instead of always returning 200 OK.

Q3. Difference between returning User and ResponseEntity<User>?

Returning User

Only returns the response body.
Status is usually 200 OK.

Returning ResponseEntity<User>

Returns body + status code + headers.